.TH FAST2BAN-REGEX "1" "October 2026" "Fast2Ban v0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fast2ban-regex \- test Fail2Ban regexes against log lines or systemd journals
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fast2ban-regex
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fILOG\fR \fIREGEX\fR [\fIIGNOREREGEX\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBfast2ban-regex\fR tests filter regexes against single log lines, log files, or
systemd journal entries, displaying matches, missed lines, and failure extractions.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-datepattern\fR <PATTERN>
Custom date pattern matching regex.
.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-encoding\fR <ENCODING>
File encoding (\fIutf-8\fR, \fIlatin-1\fR, \fIascii\fR).
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-maxlines\fR <N>
Maximum lines for multi-line regex matching.
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-journalmatch\fR <MATCH>
Journalctl match filters (e.g. \fI"_SYSTEMD_UNIT=sshd.service + _COMM=sshd"\fR).
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-log-level\fR <LEVEL>
Logging level for filter execution.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Verbose output showing capture groups.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Quiet mode.
.TP
\fB\-\-print-all-matched\fR
Print all matched log lines.
.TP
\fB\-\-print-all-missed\fR
Print all missed log lines.
.TP
\fB\-\-print-all-ignored\fR
Print all lines matching ignoreregex.
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR <FORMAT>
Machine-readable output format (\fIid\fR, \fIfid\fR, \fIip\fR, \fImsg\fR, \fIrow\fR).
.SH "SEE ALSO"
fast2ban-server(1), fast2ban-client(1), jail.conf(5)
